 "recognition_note": "The supplied six-CDR combination is an exact match to HAB13 in WO2026122589A1, first public 2026-06-11. The patent establishes HAB13 binding to HSV-1 and HSV-2 glycoprotein D, strong HSV-2 neutralization, and ADCC, but it provides no residue map, escape result, competition bin, or solved HAB13 complex. I did not inspect any native/query complex.",
 "what_separated_them": "No source localizes HAB13: the patent is about this binder but supplies phenotype only, and every residue-level map concerns another antibody or a receptor. The distribution is therefore a Tier-B prior over surfaces. What separated it was the conjunction of phenotype compatibility, conventional-Fab rather than nanobody/receptor precedent, exact handed-footprint accessibility and extent, and a duplicate-surface correction: C3, C4, and C6 are nested drawings of one receptor-overlap face and share 0.59 total probability rather than counting as three independent confirmations. C4 is the most coherent boundary within that group.",
